<div class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">SYSTEM INFORMATION</div><h1>About</h1><p>Administrator tools for article content and publication status.</p></div></div>
<section class="card about-card"><div class="card-body"><span class="stat-icon tone-blue"><%- include('partials/icon',{name:'article'}) %></span><h2>Article content management</h2><p>CONTENT DESK is an administrator-only blog content management system, developed from a WEB322 course project. Create and organize articles, manage their status, and update their cover images.</p><p>All articles, including unpublished work, belong to this private workspace. A Published label records an internal content status; it does not publish to an external website.</p><div class="about-features"><div><strong>One content library</strong><p>Search, filter and switch between a table and a visual gallery.</p></div><div><strong>Article editing</strong><p>A dedicated editor with cover previews and clear save feedback.</p></div><div><strong>Private by design</strong><p>Administrator sign-in protects the workspace and its article APIs.</p></div></div><div class="tech-note"><strong>Under the hood</strong><p>Node.js · Express · EJS · PostgreSQL · Cloudinary · Tabler</p></div></div></section>
